EZ PERMIT STANDARDS ALTERATIONS - For alterations to an Existing One Family Dwelling as per attached standard. Deviations from this standard will result in permit revocation and require submission of construction plans. Structural alteration or repair is expressly prohibited under this permit. Prohibited structural work any modifications to exterior walls, party walls, floor/roof framing or foundations, including underpinning, excavation, and removal of foundation slab. WORK IN THE BASEMENT OR CELLAR IS NOT INCLUDED ON THE EZ ALT PERMIT. Separate permits required for Mechanical, Electric and Plumbing. 
1st floor-Install new hardwood of existing floor, Remove kitchen tile install new floor, Replace four windows, all of the energy compliant contractor we use existing masonry openings, Remove and replace GWB, Replace existing kitchen cabinets, Remove and replace baseboard, Remove and replace the GWB ceiling, Install new handrail to basement stairs, Paint walls and ceiling, Add half bath;
2rd floor- Install new hardwood floor of existing floor, Build out new master bathroom with new fixtures, Build out new master bedroom, Replace 5 windows are to be energy-efficient using existing masonry opening, Frame for closets to be non-loadbearing, Remove and replace existing baseboards trim and sills, Need to replace GWB or interior partition walls Corridor and ceilings, Repair damaged handrails at stair opening, Paint entire second floor.
